 <li><strong>Days 15–45:</strong> offer ten €750 sourcing diagnostics, paid in advance. Use existing distributors as importer and seller. Cap samples, translation and supplier checks at €1,200. Do this beside the day job, with no customer promise during employed hours.</li>
 <li><strong>Days 30–60:</strong> give the buy box to Brookz advisers, BuyInside and five accountants. Request three anonymised information memoranda. Pay up to €1,500 for an independent accountant to build one normalisation workbook. Do not sign exclusivity.</li>
 <li><strong>Days 55–80:</strong> apply the workbook to three targets. Replace the seller's hours at the €90,000 CEO hurdle, stress gross profit by 10%, map working capital and call no customers without permission. Reject any file that needs post-close “synergy” to pay debt.</li>
-<li><strong>Days 75–90:</strong> spend up to €1,500 on Dutch acquisition counsel only if a target and lender both pass. Draft heads for account-owner retention, working-capital peg, seller subordination and customer-reference access. Total pre-evidence spend is capped at <strong>€4,800</strong>.</li>
+<li><strong>Days 75–90:</strong> spend up to €1,500 on Dutch acquisition counsel only if a target and lender both pass. Draft heads for account-owner retention, working-capital peg, seller subordination and customer-reference access. Total pre-evidence spend is capped at <strong>€4,800</strong>. Every euro is debited from the €10,000 non-equity allowance, leaving at most €5,200 for later lender, diligence and closing costs.</li>
 </ol>
 <p><strong>Pass:</strong> one distributor pays €750, and a lender gives a written €160,000 path that keeps total buyer cash and personal recourse within €50,000. One seller must also open records showing at least €96,000 cash before acquisition debt after replacement labour. The flat-sales model must cover senior debt at least 1.5 times, a hurdle rather than an observed covenant. <strong>Kill:</strong> no paid diagnostic after ten qualified offers; every lender breaks the €50,000 total-risk cap; or all three targets depend on the seller for a key account, qualification or ordinary decision. Passing authorises diligence, not a bid. Closing ends the day job.</p>
 </section>

