+<li><strong>Days 75–90:</strong> spend up to €1,500 on Dutch acquisition counsel only if a target and lender both pass. Draft heads for account-owner retention, working-capital peg, seller subordination and customer-reference access. Total pre-evidence spend is capped at <strong>€4,800</strong>. Every euro is debited from the €10,000 non-equity allowance, leaving at most €5,200 for later lender, diligence and closing costs.</li>
