 <p>The useful edges are narrower than “developer buys boring business.” English, Polish and Russian help qualify CEE suppliers and speak directly with parts makers. Regulatory literacy helps reject products with hidden importer duties. An engineering habit helps expose stock, quote, picking and quality failures as measurable work. The audience can produce introductions to industrial buyers and operators. None of those edges proves that this reader can retain a Dutch customer book.</p>
 <p>The Dutch-language gate is commercial. A2 is not enough for an angry local buyer, a performance conversation with an employee or a subtle price negotiation. <!-- CHECK: 05-language-gate --> The gate passes only if a Dutch account owner remains under a signed employment and retention arrangement, leads the top-customer handover and already owns routine relationships. It fails if “the team speaks Dutch” but every exception still goes to the seller. The buyer should attend those calls, improve Dutch and remain accountable. Translation is not customer ownership.</p>
-<p>Hammond Chemicals is the useful precedent elsewhere. Euston Ventures acquired the UK blender, packager and distributor of industrial solvents. Search-fund entrepreneur Jim Ward became chief executive, while the third Hammond generation stayed in leadership. <!-- CHECK: 05-precedent-deal --> The independent Companies House trace lists Hammond Chemicals Limited as active, incorporated in 1969 and engaged in wholesale of chemical products. <!-- CHECK: 05-precedent-trace --> It proves the operating shape: an outside CEO, lender-backed succession and family leaders retained.</p>
-<p>It does not prove affordability. The transaction price and cash flow were not public in the sources used here, and the acquirer had sector knowledge and institutional support. <!-- CHECK: 05-precedent-deal --> This reader should copy the retention logic, not infer a multiple. The personal constraint is equally sharp: search can run beside the job, but operation cannot. On closing day the software job ends. If employment must continue, do not sign.</p>
